fastreindex - Fast Reindex plugin for DokuWiki
==============================================

Refreshes the tag and search index after you edited, added or copied page
files directly (outside of the wiki editor). Unchanged pages are skipped.

Modes
-----
* Tags only: updates the "subject" metadata index used by the tag plugin
  (tag lists, tag links). Only pages that contain {{tag>...}} or already have
  subject metadata are processed. Much faster than a full index because it
  does not index page bodies.
* Full index: runs DokuWiki's own indexer (Indexer::addPage) for changed
  pages and updates the fulltext search index too.

Usage
-----
Admin -> Fast Reindex -> Start. Keep the page open until it finishes.
Requires admin rights. The tag plugin is optional (only used to clean tags).

Performance notes
-----------------
What is fast, and what is not:

* Tags only mode is fast. Full index mode calls the same core indexer as
  DokuWiki itself, so the time per page is about the same as the built-in
  indexing. This plugin does not make that part faster.
* What the plugin adds: batching with progress/remaining time, skipping pages
  that are already up to date, an automatic retry of failed pages, and a
  stop/resume that does not redo finished pages.
* No benchmark numbers are published yet.

Why a full index can take long:

* Every page has to be rendered to get its title, links and media, so all
  installed syntax plugins run for every page. After clearing the cache or
  copying pages from another wiki, nothing is cached and the first run pays
  this cost once. Later runs only handle changed pages.
* Large single pages dominate the run time (cost grows with page size). A few
  multi-megabyte pages can take as long as hundreds of small ones.
* Each page updates several index files with locking; antivirus real-time
  scanning of the data folder makes this noticeably slower. Excluding the wiki
  folder from real-time scanning can help.

Tips:

* Do not browse the wiki in another tab while a full index run is in progress.
  DokuWiki's own background indexer then competes for the same locks and
  single pages can fail.
* If you only need tag pages updated, use Tags only mode.
* Run Full index once after copying a wiki; afterwards only changed pages are
  processed.

Troubleshooting
---------------
* "Failed" pages are retried once automatically. When a run finishes, the
  names of failed pages (up to 100) are shown under the progress table.
* Indexer exceptions are written to the DokuWiki error log
  (data/log/error/<date>.log) as:
    fastreindex: <page>: <ExceptionClass>: <message>
* Warnings such as "Undefined array key" for date/user/description usually come
  from other plugins reading page metadata that does not exist because
  data/meta was not copied along with data/pages. They do not come from this
  plugin and are harmless for indexing.

Install
-------
Copy this folder to lib/plugins/fastreindex/ (folder name must be exactly
"fastreindex") or install through the Extension Manager.

Changelog
---------
1.0.1 (2026-10-12)
  * Fix full index mode on recent DokuWiki releases (idx_get_version() was
    removed; uses Indexer::getVersion()).
  * Log indexer exceptions to the error log instead of silently counting them.
  * Show the names of failed pages when a run finishes.
1.0.0 (2026-10-10)
  * Initial release.

